// Pre-existing "unclosed altimate_change start" false positives.
//
// census.ts's parseMarkerBlocks() flags any `altimate_change start` line with
// no matching `altimate_change end` before EOF. As of the 2026-07-18 S1
// hardening pass, buildCensus()/assembleCensus() THROWS if any unclosed
// block is found and not covered by an entry here (Codex review finding #1).
//
// 56 entries below, hand-verified: every one is a doc/test file that mentions
// the `altimate_change start`/`altimate_change end` marker syntax literally
// (as example text, a string literal in a test fixture, or documentation
// prose) rather than an actual unmatched marker wrapping real code. New
// genuinely-unclosed markers must NOT be added here — fix the marker (add a
// matching `altimate_change end`) instead.
//
// NOTE: the `script/upstream/` package itself (including this file) is
// currently untracked in git, so a `census.ts --json` run against `--ours
// HEAD` (the tool's only supported mode) cannot see these files at all and
// will report every entry below whose `file` lives under `script/upstream/`,
// `docs/internal/census/`, or `.claude/commands/consolidate-test-prs.md` as
// "did not match any unclosed block this run" — that is expected while these
// files are uncommitted, not a sign of a stale line number. Entries for
// those paths were instead verified directly by importing `parseMarkerBlocks`
// and running it against the real working-tree file content. Re-verify them
// against a live `census.ts --json` run once this package is committed.
